    "body": "## What Changed\n\nPublish fallback canonical-session JSON recordings through the existing atomic writer, so readers see a complete snapshot and a failed write keeps the previously saved session history.\n\nThe writer gains an opt-in `preserveExistingMode` option. Recording files keep their existing POSIX read/write/execute permission bits; newly created recordings retain the previous `0666 & ~umask` behavior. Other atomic-writer callers keep their current defaults. Recording reads also use the existing bounded Windows sharing retry.\n\n## Why This Change\n\nThe fallback currently writes directly to the published JSON file. If a write partially succeeds and then fails, for example with `ENOSPC`, the previous recording has already been truncated. A later save treats the invalid JSON as a missing recording and loses the accumulated history. During an initial write, readers can also observe an incomplete file.\n\nThe regression tests inject a failure after writing actual partial bytes. They check visibility during the write, preservation after failure, temporary-file cleanup, and recovery on the next successful save for both fallback entry paths.\n\n## Testing Done\n\n- Linux Node 18, 20 and 22, macOS Node 22, and Windows Node 22: all four partial-write regressions fail against exact base `8abdf329` and pass against candidate `0083c6e8`.\n- The POSIX permission control passes before and after the change on Linux and macOS, including creation umask and replacement of files with `0600`, `0640`, and `0660` permissions.\n- Full `npm test` on clean Ubuntu / Node 22: candidate **490/490 test files pass**, with complete execution integrity. The runner reports 9,998 passing assertions.\n- The exact-base full run completes **488 passed / 1 failed**. Its failure is `lib/claude-settings.test.js`, “atomic settings updates reject parent replacement at rename,” at the staging-descriptor assertion. That test and its settings implementation are unchanged by this PR; this is not claimed as a fix for that failure.\n- Changed-file ESLint passes. Six related test files pass. Combined changed-source coverage is **97.35% lines/statements, 85.15% branches, 100% functions**.\n- Local focused tests and the same six-file coverage run pass.\n- [Exact-base/candidate full suites and five platform/runtime jobs](https://github.com/Afloat16/ECC/actions/runs/43973080665).\n\n- [ ] Manual testing completed\n- [ ] Automated full suite passes locally (`node tests/run-all.js`)\n- [x] Edge cases considered and tested\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] `fix:` Bug fix\n\n## Security & Quality Checklist\n\n- [x] No secrets or API keys committed\n- [x] No sensitive data exposed in regression fixtures\n- [x] Follows conventional commits format\n- [x] Independent code and regression-test review completed\n\nAtomic publication does not serialize multiple concurrent read/modify/write operations; multi-writer history merging is outside this change. The existing handling of a permanently unreadable or invalid recording remains unchanged.\n\nThe three-file patch has no dependency, package manifest, shell-script, or published-path changes.\n",
